marinaMoji Debian source notes
==============================

Building this package
---------------------

1. Symlink this tree to the repository root as `debian/` (see README.md).
2. Install Build-Depends from debian/control, plus a Bazelisk binary that
   can provide the Bazel version pinned in src/.bazeliskrc (currently
   9.0.2). Distro `bazel` packages are often too old; prefer Bazelisk.
3. Run `dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b` on a machine **with network**.

The Bazel build downloads BCR modules and several http_archive /
http_file dependencies declared in src/MODULE.bazel. That is fine for
local maintainer experiments and mirrors the Arch `marinamoji` PKGBUILD,
but it is incompatible with Debian's clean chroot builds (`sbuild`),
which have no network.

Offline builds
--------------

Tracked as https://github.com/marinaMoji/marinaMoji/issues/53.

**Current approach:** Bazel [vendor mode](https://bazel.build/external/vendor).

1. On a networked machine, run
   `bash packaging/debian/offline/vendor_deps.sh`
   (add `-- --config oss_linux --config release_build` on Linux).
   That fills `packaging/debian/vendor/` (gitignored).
2. Symlink `packaging/debian` → `debian/` at the repo root.
3. Build with `dpkg-buildpackage` / `verify_offline.sh`. `debian/rules`
   detects `debian/vendor/` and passes `--vendor_dir`,
   `--repository_disable_download`, and `--lockfile_mode=error`.

See `packaging/debian/offline/README.md` for details and the network
dependency inventory.

Still open before NEW:

* Decide how the large vendor tree ships (orig tarball vs separate
  component) and any DFSG `Files-Excluded` / `+dfsg` repack.
* Optional later: Debian-mozc-style `--override_module` stubs onto
  system `-dev` packages to shrink the tree.

Copyright inventory
-------------------

debian/copyright is the source-package DEP-5 starting point. The
machine-readable file shipped inside today's binary .deb (install-tree
paths) remains packaging/linux/data/copyright. Aligning source paths and
a Files-Excluded repack story is part of #52 / #53.

Package split
-------------

Debian mozc ships mozc-server, mozc-data, ibus-mozc, etc. marinaMoji
currently installs one package named marinamoji. Splitting is
https://github.com/marinaMoji/marinaMoji/issues/59 and is deliberately
out of scope for the first scaffold.
